      "id": "pg20005",
      "elType": "widget",
      "widgetType": "accordion",
      "settings": {
       "tabs": [
        {
         "tab_title": "Is Malta a good destination for international students?",
         "tab_content": "<p>Yes. English is an official language in Malta, schools offer EU-recognised qualifications, and students enjoy a safe, multicultural Mediterranean lifestyle.</p>",
         "_id": "pgq0000"
        },
        {
         "tab_title": "Do I need a visa to study in Malta?",
         "tab_content": "<p>Students from the EU do not need a visa. Most students from outside the EU need a student visa and a residence permit for courses longer than 90 days. Requirements depend on your nationality and your course, and we help you prepare your application.</p>",
         "_id": "pgq0001"
        },
        {
         "tab_title": "How much does it cost to study in Malta?",
         "tab_content": "<p>It depends on the school and programme. For example, our 12-month Professional English Programme has a launch price of €3,950. See our <a href=\"https://outreachstudy.eu/studying-in-malta-on-a-budget-a-guide-to-affordability-in-malta/\">guide to the cost of studying in Malta</a> for living costs.</p>",
         "_id": "pgq0002"
        },
        {
         "tab_title": "What are the entry requirements?",
         "tab_content": "<p>They depend on the programme level. Read our <a href=\"https://outreachstudy.eu/study-in-malta-requirements/\">guide to study in Malta requirements</a>, or book a free consultation and we check your documents with you.</p>",
         "_id": "pgq0003"
        }
       ]
      },
      "elements": []
     }
    ],
